<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Progressive Party (Guyana)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950</span> · Also known as PPP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-progressive-party-the-gambia">People's Progressive Party</a> is a political party of Guyana founded in 1950 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheddi-jagan">Cheddi Jagan</a>, Janet Jagan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forbes-burnham">Forbes Burnham</a>. It won the 1953 elections in British Guiana, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> suspended the constitution after 133 days, fearing a communist government. After Burnham's breakaway in 1955 it drew its support mainly from Indo-Guyanese voters, and it has governed Guyana for long periods since 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-progressive-party-guyana.jpg" alt="People's Progressive Party (Guyana)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prez001 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:People%27s_Progressive_Party-Civic_Flag_(Guyana).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
